in this video i'll be showing you all  the secrets for how to fish  in animal crossing new horizons this is  a video that will be great for beginners  of the game who want to know more about  one of the most popular activities in  animal crossing it's also a great way to  make bells  we'll start out covering the basics of  fishing how to catch different types of  fish  and then an extra special tip on a  unique way to use  fish bait and we're starting right now  people of the international retro  raccoon tour here and welcome back to  another animal crossing new horizons  video  if you guys are new here we post two  gaming videos each week and if you enjoy  the video today i'd love for you to  subscribe to the channel  but only if you love the video of course  so where do we begin with  fishing well for starters it's been one  of the most popular activities since all  the way back to the original animal  crossing game for the nintendo gamecube  and personally it's one of my favorite  things to do in the game  it's relatively simple to get started  with fishing but it can be difficult to  fully master don't worry we're going to  cover it all here today  first you'll need to obtain a fishing  rod you can either purchase one at  nook's cranny using bells or you can  craft one instead  you'll get the flimsy fishing rod diy  recipe from tom nook fairly early in the  game  if you don't have it yet just keep  completing your objectives from tom nook  and when he lets you know about a free  crafting workshop  make sure you take him up on the offer  the flimsy fishing rod is fairly easy to  craft as it only requires five tree  branches  just walk around shaking trees until you  get five this particular rod will break  after catching just 10 fish but don't  worry  you'll unlock better options as you  continue to play through the game  once you have your fishing rod head over  to any body of water and start looking  for fish  you'll want to make sure you walk  instead of run because running often  scares fish away  they come in several different shadow  sizes some have fins and some are  longer and thinner these shadow sizes  are really only important when you're  going after  a specific fish but more on that in just  a bit  for now position yourself in front of  the shadow and press  a to cast your line if it's not anywhere  close to the fish's mouth then press  a again to just reel it back in you can  then reposition  and cast again this can take a little  bit to get used to but eventually you'll  start to understand the angles and be  able to position yourself just right on  the first or second try  once you get the fishing line in the eye  side of the fish wait  do not press a and attempt to reel back  you'll see the fish get closer  and closer and then start to nibble  you'll know it's nibbling because of the  little bobber in the water  now this is where things get interesting  sometimes the fish will bite immediately  other times they'll take a few nibbles  first what you're really looking for is  the bobber going  all the way under a stronger vibration  from your controller  and a slightly different sound as the  bobber goes down  under the water  as soon as this happens press and hold a  keep holding the button until you reel  in the fish and congratulations you just  caught your first fish  fishing and animal crossing is purely  about timing  if you're quick enough pressing a you'll  catch the fish every time  press it too early or too late though  and you'll lose out on the fish  it's a pretty simple process but you  should know that rare fish usually  require more precise  timing to be honest the easiest way to  catch the fish  is to close your eyes no i'm serious  close your eyes  at least once you have the bobber in  their line of sight closing your eyes  actually helps in a few different ways  first this removes the element of you  possibly getting faked out by a fish  just going in for a nibble now you're  just listening for the special water  kerplunk sound that only happens when  the fish bites  it sounds like this  and believe it or not the sound actually  comes ever so slightly before  the visual indicator with the bobber  going underwater  some people don't have any trouble at  all either way but if you find yourself  frequently missing some of the rare fish  you may want to try the closing your  eyes trick as someone who's been fishing  in animal crossing games for years i  have to say it's honestly  easier to close your eyes when you're  doing the fishing now when it comes to  catching different types of fish there  are two things you need to know  the first thing is that many fish are  seasonal in animal crossing  meaning they're only available to catch  during certain months of the year  the animal crossing fandom wiki is a  great place to see this information  i also put out a little guide each month  to help you quickly see all the new fish  you can find it on my twitter account or  in my discord  i'll put a link to all of these down in  the description below  but it's not just about seasonality the  fish  also spawn in specific locations and at  specific times of the day  there's the sea rivers and ponds there  are also  additional special locations such as the  pier river mouth  clifftop rivers and clifftop ponds  all of this information is also in the  monthly guide i post  as well as on the wiki so if you're  looking to catch every fish you'll need  to get comfortable with  all the locations in the game as well as  knowing which fish you can catch  during specific months and specific  times of the day  if you only play at a certain time each  day let's say in the morning  then you'll have to change your play  habits to catch fish that only spawn  during the evening hours  or you can always time travel if that's  something you're okay with doing  you'll most likely want to donate new  fish to your museum first  but fish are also a great way to make  bells especially when cj comes to town  as he'll pay you 50 percent more than  the same fish at nook's cranny  now with so many rare fish only spawning  at specific locations  you'll want to get familiar with fish  bait you can craft one fish bait for  every one manila clam you find  on the beach these are the little  shadows you see fairly often in the sand  now i mentioned an extra special tip  regarding fish bait and  something i only learned just recently  despite playing the game  since launch okay so first the basics of  fish bait they're pretty simple  walk up to any body of water toss it out  and a fish will appear  from there it's basically what we talked  about before but let's say you're going  after a specific fish like a blue marlin  now the blue marlin only spawns at the  pier as a huge  shadow so if you throw out fish baiting  at a small shadow there's really no  point in catching that fish  now what i would used to do is i would  run around scared away and then use  another fish bait very often though  using this method it would give me the  exact  same fish and also take up extra time  but here's the trick instead of scaring  the fish away just throw out another  fish  bait with the fish already there  the bait hitting the water will scare  that fish away and a new fish will still  spawn in  of course you use a lot more bait this  way but if you're going after a specific  fish this method is far  more time efficient after you catch all  the fish in the game you'll get the diy  recipe for the golden fishing rod  no you will not see me with the golden  fishing rod just yet because at the time  i'm recording this video  it's currently impossible to obtain the  fishing rod without  time traveling and i'm not a time  traveler no worries if you are though  you do you i mentioned earlier how i  hoped you'd subscribed if you enjoyed  the video  so if you want to see more animal  crossing content like this hit that  subscribe button and don't forget to  ring the notification  bell also if you're a beginner i have  prepared a full  animal crossing beginners playlist that  i'll link to here on the right side of  your page  be sure and check it out thanks so much  for watching i'll talk to you again soon
 

